@startuml
title Components and layers — current and proposed
top to bottom direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

package "Presentation / entry point" {
  component "app.py\nStreamlit entry point\nIMPLEMENTED" as Entry
  component "view.py\nwidgets + rendering\nIMPLEMENTED" as View
}
package "Application" {
  component "controller.py\ncalculate(CombatInput, rng)\nIMPLEMENTED: legacy delegation" as Controller
  component "ShootingService\nPLANNED" as Service
}
package "Domain" {
  component "model.py\nCombatInput / CombatResult\nabstract simulation\nIMPLEMENTED: legacy" as Model
  component "domain/inputs.py\nShootingSituation + facts\nIMPLEMENTED: data only" as Inputs
  component "domain/to_hit.py\nToHitTarget\nIMPLEMENTED: typed value" as ToHit
  component "domain/firepower.py\nFirepowerTarget\nIMPLEMENTED: typed value" as Firepower
  component "domain/dice.py\nDieRoller protocol\nIMPLEMENTED: port only" as Dice
  component "hit distribution / pinning / save / kill resolvers\nPLANNED; rule stages UNRESOLVED" as Resolvers
}
component "NumPy\nIMPLEMENTED external dependency" as NumPy

Entry --> View : render_inputs / render_results
Entry --> Controller : calculate
View --> Model : CombatInput / CombatResult
Controller --> Model : simulate
Model --> NumPy : sampling
View --> NumPy : histogram + mean/min/max
Inputs --> ToHit
Inputs --> Firepower
Service ..> Inputs : future orchestration
Service ..> Resolvers : future orchestration
Resolvers ..> Dice : planned injected roll port

note right of Inputs
No Weapon or Unit identity object.
No current dependency from legacy MVC
to these V4 input value types.
end note
@enduml
